Hi Gary,

By "not capturing the observed locations most distant from the colony" are you talking about the locations not falling into the 95% coverage area? If so, this is normal with abundant data - that only 95% of the locations fall within the 95% coverage area. With limited amounts of autocorrelated data, the coverage area includes more observed data, but is less certain.

Best,
Chris

